-- title:
--   Descent of the nodal normal form uv=t, 𝔪=(u,v)
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian local domain of some universe $u$ whose maximal ideal is generated by a single element $\varpi$, so $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi)$, with $\varpi \neq 0$. Write $R_\varpi$ for the crossing model [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel A ϖ`](def/ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel.html#L15), namely the quotient of the ring of formal power series in two variables $A\langle\!\langle X_0, X_1\rangle\!\rangle$ (multivariate power series indexed by `Fin 2`) by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - \varpi$, where $\varpi$ is viewed as a constant power series. Let $O$ be a Noetherian local ring in the same universe, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto $R_\varpi$. Let $t \in O$ be an element whose image in the completion is carried by $e$ to [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.const ϖ ϖ`](def/ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel.html#L29), the class of the constant power series $\varpi$ (equivalently, by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.U_mul_V`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.U_mul_V), the class of $X_0X_1$). Assume finally that the set of minimal primes of the ideal $tO$ is not a subsingleton, i.e. $tO$ has at least two distinct minimal primes. Then there exist $u, v \in O$ with $uv = t$ and $\mathfrak m_O = (u,v)$.
--
--   This is the descent, from the completion to the ring itself, of the normal form of a node: a ring whose completion is the crossing model $A\langle\!\langle U,V\rangle\!\rangle/(UV-\varpi)$ with $t$ corresponding to $UV$, and in which $t$ cuts out at least two branches, already carries an algebraic factorisation $t = uv$ with $u, v$ generating the maximal ideal. It is used in the analysis of the local structure at the singular points of the special fibre of an integral model of the modular curve, through [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_mul_eq_and_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_not_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_mul_eq_and_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_not_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul); the argument itself is commutative algebra, resting on the regularity, Krull dimension two, factoriality and the computation of the minimal primes of $UV$ in the crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_mul_eq_and_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
